# StoreDesk Master Prompt

Before planning or changing code, read and follow the full specification in **`AGENTS.md`** at the workspace root (`StoreDesk/AGENTS.md`).

For multi-agent delivery (work orders, handoffs, role routing), also read **`.cursor/TEAM.md`**. Use Cursor + Codex only — no `.claude/`.

## Parent repository with submodules

This is the **StoreDesk parent repo**. App code lives in Git submodules:

- `store-desk-electron/` — StoreDesk desktop
- `store-desk-server/` — StoreDesk Server (edge API)
- `store-desk-mobile/` — StoreDesk Mobile
- `store-desk-web/` — StoreDesk Web (marketing + license admin on Vercel)
- `store-desk-cloud-backend/` — Cloud Hub (WSS rooms; Epic 1)

Rules:

- **Do not merge submodules** into the parent as normal tracked files.
- **Do not convert** to npm/pnpm monorepo.
- **Do not remove** `.gitmodules` or submodule metadata manually.
- Commit app changes **inside the submodule**, push, then update the parent submodule pointer.
- Clone with `--recurse-submodules` or run `git submodule update --init --recursive`.

## Product names

- **StoreDesk** — Electron desktop admin app (`store-desk-electron/`)
- **StoreDesk Server** — Edge Node.js + Express + local MongoDB (`store-desk-server/`)
- **StoreDesk Mobile** — Flutter phone app (`store-desk-mobile/`). Prefer this name (legacy: Buddy).
- **StoreDesk Web** — Next.js marketing + store license control plane (`store-desk-web/`)

## Non-negotiable scope

**In scope:** products, variants, UPC/barcode lookup, vendors, vendor price comparison, invoice upload/review, suggested selling prices, mobile scanning, mobile invoice upload, store licenses/cloud hub (migration), future lottery setup placeholder.

**Never build:** stock quantity, inventory counts, add/reduce stock, low stock, reorder levels, warehouse locations, stock movements, inventory adjustment, `Inventory` model, `StockMovement` model, stock APIs.

## Architecture rules

- **Edge-first catalog:** store catalog, Commander, and invoices stay on the store PC (local Mongo). Atlas holds **licenses / store registry / agent keys only** (~512MB M0).
- **Cloud Hub (planned):** Desktop and Mobile may connect via outbound WSS through Cloud Run; keep `listen(4310)` until dual-mode is proven.
- **No Redis** for Phase 0–1 Hub unless explicitly added later (Memorystore).
- StoreDesk Server listens on **port 4310** and **0.0.0.0** for LAN mobile access (current mode).
- Desktop connects to `http://localhost:4310` in local mode.
- Mobile connects to `http://LAN_IP:4310` in LAN mode — never `localhost` on the phone.
- StoreDesk Mobile connects only to StoreDesk Server (or Cloud Hub later) — never directly to MongoDB.
- Never save raw invoice extraction as final vendor price; always require review before creating `VendorPrice`.
- Preserve vendor price history; do not silently overwrite old prices.
- Brand colors: primary `#1A63F4`, secondary `#00A87B` (see `brand-kit/`).
- Use centralized theme tokens — do not hardcode random colors in pages.
- Keep business logic in services, not UI pages.

## Checks after major changes

```txt
Electron (store-desk-electron): npm run ci
Server (store-desk-server):       npm run ci
Mobile (store-desk-mobile):       npm run ci   # requires Flutter locally
```

If Flutter is not installed, document verification as pending — do not fake success.

## Implementation priority

Follow the sprint order in root `AGENTS.md`. Inspect the repo and existing READMEs before large refactors. Preserve passing checks unless fixing them.
